# Next.js App Router Standards

## File Organization

- Use App Router structure (`app/` directory)
- Route files: `page.tsx` for pages, `layout.tsx` for layouts
- Server Components by default, use `'use client'` only when needed
- Colocate components, styles, and utilities with routes

## Server vs Client Components

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Server Component (default)
export default async function BookingPage() {
  const bookings = await getBookings();
  return <BookingList bookings={bookings} />;
}

// ✅ GOOD - Client Component (only when needed)
'use client';
export function BookingForm() {
  const [date, setDate] = useState(new Date());
  // Interactive logic here
}
```

## Data Fetching

- Use `async/await` in Server Components
- Fetch data directly in Server Components, not in `useEffect`
- Use `fetch` with proper caching strategies

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
async function getBookings() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/bookings', {
    next: { revalidate: 3600 } // ISR
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

## Metadata and SEO

- Export `metadata` object from page files
- Use dynamic metadata when needed

```tsx
export const metadata = {
  title: 'Reservar Cita - Barbería',
  description: 'Sistema de reservas para barbería',
};
```
